426: 
427: **Hub.**
428: 
429: - Title "Language Games" and the subtitle "Learn English by playing Wittgenstein's language-games."
430: - A Continue strip, for example "Slab! · round 7 · your 2 orders are saved".
431: - One card per game: key art, name, a one-line promise ("Give orders. Watch them get built."), the English target
432:   ("Plurals, articles, *on/under*"), and progress.
433: - Footer: Notebook · Sources · Notes · About.
434: 
435: **Round screen (phone, 390×844, no page scroll):**
436: 
437: ```
438: ┌──────────────────────────────┐
439: │ ← Slab!     Round 3/5     ?  │  top bar, 48 px
440: ├──────────────────────────────┤
441: │                              │
442: │   stage (art + SVG state)    │  ~40% of height, 3:2
443: │                              │
444: ├──────────────────────────────┤
445: │ B: "Which slab?"             │  response line (aria-live)
446: ├──────────────────────────────┤
447: │ [Put] [the] [red] [slab] [⌫] │  sentence line
448: ├──────────────────────────────┤
449: │ put bring a the two red grey │  tile tray: wraps, and
450: │ pillar pillars beam slab on  │  scrolls inside itself
451: │ there👉                      │  if it overflows
452: ├──────────────────────────────┤
453: │ Orders 1 · par 2     [Send ▶]│  48 px primary action
454: └──────────────────────────────┘
455: ```
456: 
457: On desktop (1440×900), the stage takes the left 60% and the composer and order history the right 40%, at a
458: maximum width of 1200 px.
459: 
460: **Feedback line.** After each submission, at most two lines:
461: 
462: - What happened, e.g. "B put the beam *under* the pillars".
463: - The English note, e.g. "*on* = on top of; *under* = below".
464: - A § chip that opens the source card.
465: 
466: **Round result.** Marks (●●○), a one-line debrief that links what you did to the passage, the English notes, and
467: a "Next round" button.
468: 
469: **Session summary.**
470: 
471: - Marks for the 5 rounds, the passages you enacted (as chips), and the English points you practised.
472: - Buttons: *Next game*, *5 more*, *Notebook*.
473: - No comparison with other players.
474: 
475: **Notebook.** Two tabs.
476: 
477: - *Passages*: one page per passage you acted out, with:
478:   - the § reference and our paraphrase;
479:   - a short quote, with the translator credited;
480:   - "What you did", filled in from your own round ("You trained the pupil with *an egg* and *a unicorn*");
481:   - a link to the text.
482: - *English*: the notes you received, each with the rule and your corrected sentence.
483: - Empty state: "Play a round; the passages you act out will appear here."
484: 
485: **States.**
486: 
487: - *First run* (no progress): the hub highlights Slab!.
488: - *Resume*: the in-progress round and the half-built sentence come back after a reload.
489: - *Partial*: progress is shown per game.
490: - *Complete*: all rounds are done. Any round can be replayed, with no nagging.
491: - *Storage unavailable* (private mode, full quota): play still works in memory, with a quiet notice.
492: - *Corrupt storage*: the data is backed up and reset, with a one-line notice.
493: 
494: ### 2.5 Interaction and accessibility rules
495: 
496: - **Tap or keyboard, never drag-only.**
497:   - Tiles are buttons and are reusable: they work as a palette, not as single-use tokens.
498:   - Tab moves into the tray, arrow keys move within it, Enter or Space adds a tile, and Backspace removes the
499:     last one.
500:   - Enter on the sentence line sends it.
501: - **Every stage state has a text twin**, e.g. "Site: red pillar at column 2; grey beam on the pillars". It is
502:   announced in an `aria-live` region, and every stage SVG has a `<title>`.
503: - **Colour is never the only cue.** Stones carry a pattern and a label, and lit cards also get a check icon.
504: - **Size, focus, contrast and motion.**
505:   - Touch targets are at least 44 px.
506:   - Focus rings are visible (a 2 px ink outline with a paper-coloured offset).
507:   - Contrast meets AA (§4.2).
508:   - With `prefers-reduced-motion`, there are no topple or fly animations: the new state appears at once,
509:     together with its text twin.
510: - **Text.** One idea per line, B1 wording in the UI, and no idioms in instructions.
511: 
512: ## 3. Content model and volume
513: 
514: ### 3.1 Files
515: 
516: All content is typed data. It is validated with zod at build time and in tests, and no round lives in JSX.
517: 
518: | File | What it holds |
519: |---|---|
520: | `content/sources.json` | Citation registry (§3.4) |
521: | `content/english.json` | English-target registry: id, name, rule (≤200 chars), a right example and a wrong one, and an optional note for Chinese speakers |
522: | `content/art.json` | Image registry: key, src, width, height, alt |
523: | `content/rounds/slab.json`, `go-on.json`, `family.json` (+ `logical-space.json`) | Rounds, one file per game |
524: | `content/family-concepts.json` | Cards and features shared by the Family Likeness rounds |
525: | `content/notes/*.mdx` | Notes articles |
526: | `content/AUTHORING.md` | How to add a round (linked from the README, B16) |
527: 
528: ### 3.2 Fields shared by every round
529: 
530: | Field | Type | Rule |
531: |---|---|---|
532: | `id` | string | Stable kebab-case, never reused (progress is keyed by it) |
533: | `game` | `slab` \| `go-on` \| `family` \| `logical-space` | Discriminator for the payload |
534: | `level`, `order` | int | Level 1-4; position within the game |
535: | `title` | string | ≤40 chars |
536: | `cefr` | `B1` \| `B2` | Level of the round's English |
537: | `englishTargets` | string[] | ≥1 id from `english.json`; the feedback text comes from there |
538: | `citations` | `{ sourceId, role: "enacted" \| "context" }[]` | ≥1 with role `enacted`; every source must be `verified` |
539: | `intro` | string? | ≤140 chars, shown before the round |
540: | `debrief` | string | ≤280 chars, in our words: connects what the player did to the passage |
541: | `par` | int? | Required for Slab!, Go On! and Logical Space; checked by the solver test |
542: | `solution` | game-specific | Used by the solver test and by the e2e players |
543: | `art` | `{ stage?, cards? }` | Keys into `art.json` |
544: | `status` | `draft` \| `reviewed` | Only `reviewed` rounds ship |
545: | `payload` | game-specific | See §3.3 |
546: 

