586: ```
587: 
588: **Go On!** fields:
589: 
590: - `task`: the instruction line.
591: - `ways [{id, label, rank, correct?}]`: exactly one way is `correct`; rank 1 is the pupil's first guess.
592: - `items [{id, prompt, out: {wayId: answer}, why}]`: `why` explains the correct form in English terms.
593: - `deck`: the example cards the teacher can show.
594: - `exam`: 5 item ids, disjoint from `deck`.
595: - `explain {text, keeps: [wayIds]}`: how the pupil reads the rule statement.
596: - `twist {prompt, accepted, call: "correct" | "both-in-use", why}`.
