668: 
669: What the data implies:
670: 
671: - *Winner* is true for 4 of 6 cards, so the best claim is *most*. *Skill* is 5/6, also *most*. *Compete*, *luck*,
672:   *cards*, *ball* and *alone* each come to some/not all.
673: - No feature is shared by all six cards.
674: - A thread exists through all six cards: football–chess (*compete*) → chess–poker (*winner*) → poker–patience
675:   (*cards*) → patience–wall (*alone*) → wall–ring (*amuse*).
676: 
677: Quantifier truth uses only definite values. Blurred cards count neither for nor against a claim.
678: 
679: | Quantifier | True when (k of n cards have the feature) | Best choice when |
680: |---|---|---|
681: | *all* | k = n | k = n |
682: | *most* | n/2 < k < n | n/2 < k < n |
683: | *some* / *not all* | 1 ≤ k < n | 1 ≤ k ≤ n/2 |
684: | *no* | k = 0 | k = 0 |
