693: ### 3.4 Citation registry and quoting policy
694: 
695: `sources.json` entry fields:
696: 
697: | Field | Rule |
698: |---|---|
699: | `id` | e.g. `PI-185`, `TLP-4.461`, `OC-115`, `BB-ts309-27` |
700: | `work`, `ref` | e.g. `PI`, "PI §185"; or `BB`, "BB, Ts-309 p. 27" |
701: | `paraphrase` | Our words, ≤220 chars. This is what is shown by default |
702: | `quote` | Optional, ≤25 words |
703: | `quoteSource` | Required whenever there is a quote: "trans. C. K. Ogden (1922)", "our translation of the German", or "Wittgenstein's own English (BB, dictated 1933-34)" |
704: | `url` | A reading link: LWP (wittgensteinproject.org) for PI, OC and BB; Klement's side-by-side edition (people.umass.edu/klement/tlp/) for the TLP |
705: | `verified` | `{ against, date }`. Required to ship; a content test fails on any unverified source |
706: 
707: **Quoting policy.**
708: 
709: - Paraphrase is the default.
710: - TLP quotes use Ogden's 1922 translation, which is in the public domain in the US.
711: - PI, OC and PPF quotes are our own short translations of the German original, labelled as such. We do not
712:   reproduce the Anscombe or Hacker & Schulte wording, which is under copyright; the acceptor notes this too.
713: - At most one quote of 25 words or fewer per passage. Never a full paragraph.
714: 
715: **Seed registry: checked during planning** against the German text of PI Part I, OC and the BB typescript Ts-309
716: on LWP, and against Klement's TLP.
